/-!
# The exceptional K action in the SL₃ closure argument

The original K acts on U/Z(U). The special-structure conclusions discharge
both action-kernel bounds. The complete preceding source alternatives reduce
strict L₁<K to q=4, rank eight and case (1), and the action realizes
K/O₂,Z(K) as a section of GL₈(2).

The odd-extension obstruction excludes this section for every surviving
case (1), proving K=L₁ on the original geometry. The marked SL₃,
special-structure and exact preceding Chapter 11 conclusions remain explicit
inputs to this conditional source step. The outer 11.5.7 assembly belongs
to qt-d-1222-sl3-block-exceptional.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.5.7, refs/quasithin.pdf, printed p.782.
-/
